ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Wilder Series: The Wilder Loop","url":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/events/316616155/","description":"**Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our website.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/wilder-loop-fall-26)**\n\n**The loop is back and more wild than ever!**\n\nFor those unfamiliar, The Wilder Loop is 16 km of remote, rugged terrain through one of Ontario’s most untouched landscapes. Right from the start, the trail throws you into the wild: the first 5 km have everything we love about backcountry hiking; twisting forest paths, sweeping granite ridges, narrow boardwalks, and multiple beaver dams to scramble across. No two kilometers are the same, and every twist in the trail feels like a secret waiting to be found.\n\nOnce we hit the loop section, things get much quieter. This part of the park sees very few visitors as human footprints give way to moose tracks, and the rustling in the brush might just be one of the many beavers that call this area home.\n\nThough the total elevation gain is relatively modest (about 260 m over the whole route), the trail’s difficulty comes from its remoteness, terrain, and ever-changing conditions. That said, for those willing to take it on, the reward is huge: sweeping views, total solitude, an unfiltered experience of Ontario’s boreal beauty... and a well-earned sense of pride by the time we make it back to the trailhead.\n\n***Secret Location***\nThis is one of Wilderness Union's 'secret' hikes. As a group, we visit some truly special spots that are undiscovered by the wider world. We like to keep them pristine and only share them among our members- we ask that you do the same! We reveal the location to registered members in the days before the trip.\n\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provide feedback, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\n\n**Highlights**\n**Untouched Wilderness:** Step into a landscape that feels frozen in time; wild, windswept, and wonderfully remote. Just you, the forest, and the sound of your boots on the trail.\n**Wildlife Spotting:** Bears, moose, beavers and loons are just some of the creatures that call this area home. You'll have a chance to spot some from a safe distance for a magical encounter.\n**Beaver Dam Crossings:** The area we're visiting is shaped by beavers. Tiptoe across nature’s original bridges- muddy, meticulously built, and surprisingly sturdy\n\n**Event cost: $60+HST. $50 optional transport also available. Please register [here.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/wilder-loop-fall-26)**\n\n**About Wilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps you find your people.\n\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The group is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada and abroad.\n\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not overwhelming!\n\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***","startDate":"2026-10-17T10:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":", Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/wildernessunion/"},"performer":"Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Fall Colours Canoe trip to Kawartha Highlands Provincial Park","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/events/316562323/","description":"This is a trip to view the back country Ontario during prime fall colours.\n\nThis is a one-night trip. We will paddle into the interior and camp for the night.\nThere are 2 small portage.\n\nCamp sites and canoes will be reserved. Food will be provided and carpooling arranged. You do not need to bring any food.\n\nWe will be asking for a $50 deposit via paypal or bank email transfer to keep your spot since I need to reserve the sites and canoes ahead of time. I will send out a note with further information to those who sign up. See paypal and bank email transfer info under \"COSTS\" below.\nRSVP REQUIREMENTS\n\nRSVP \"Going\" if you are sure you can attend, are able to meet the difficulty requirement, bring what is needed and have reviewed the costs associated with this event.\nEVENT DETAILS\nDifficulty: Easy to Moderate - You are able to paddle 3-4 hours per day and are reasonably fit.\n\nWhat to Bring:\nHat, Personal water bottle, 2 or 3 dry bags or garbage bags (to use for your clothes & sleeping bag) Put the garbage bag inside to line you backpack. Put another one inside your sleeping bag case to line that.\nWaterproof Coat.\nList of Clothing : Hat, swimsuit, sweaters or sweatshirts (it will get cold in the evenings), jeans or long pants, 1 towel, 2 pairs shoes - 1 for dry hiking and 1 for wet stuff. Wet shoes need to be secure, flip flops and loose sandals may get stuck in the mud.\nbowl, cup, spoon, fork, sun glasses, flashlight or strong headlamp,\nToiletries: Toilet paper, sunscreen, bug spray.\nWhen you pack your stuff, if you can pack everything in one pack, portaging will be much easier!\nOther camping items:\nBackpack, Sleeping bag (suitable for cold weather), sleeping pad or mattress\n\nGETTING THERE\nDrivers will be notified by the organizer where to meet and pick up passengers. Drivers will be sent complete directions as to where, when and who to meet and directions to the Park.\nPlease sign up for the carpool here:\n\nCOSTS\nOther: 50 deposit to remain on going list. Total cost between 180 and $220. This cost includes all gas, camp fees, food and canoe rentals. The balance is payable at the end of the trip when we calculate the costs owed by each member.\nHOW TO PAY: contact Pedro for paypal account and e-mail address\nINTRODUCTION TO CANOEING\nPlease review the following safety videos:\n(You don't need to kneel, sitting is fine for this type of trip. The other safety tips are good)\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PrjXT9bAB6c](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PrjXT9bAB6c)\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sTtFSpelQk4](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sTtFSpelQk4)\n[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_zHSfEhEqkU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_zHSfEhEqkU)\nPlease ALWAYS check your email or the event post in the evening or in the morning prior to the event for cancellation, rescheduling or last minute changes.\nPlease Note: You are required to respond to Meetup messages in a timely manner. The messages may be on the comment board below, private message, or through the email address you have registered with [Meetup.com.](http://Meetup.com.)","startDate":"2026-10-17T11:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Vibe & Wander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gta-vibe-and-wander-com/"},"performer":"Vibe & Wander"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🚐 Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake Road Trip!  Saturday, October 17","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/events/313710666/","description":"**🚐 Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake Road Trip!**\n**Saturday, October 17**\n\nLet’s hit the road for another Doors Open adventure! We’ll be heading to beautiful **Doors Open Niagara-on-the-Lake** to explore historic buildings, cultural sites, and hidden spaces that are rarely open to the public.\nNick has been a **Doors Open Toronto volunteer for over two decades**, and he always enjoys checking out Doors Open events in other cities. Niagara-on-the-Lake is known for its incredible heritage architecture, charming streets, and fascinating history—making it a perfect destination for a Doors Open day trip.\n\n***\n\n### 🏛️ What is Doors Open?\n\nIf you’ve never attended before, **Doors Open** is a free architectural and cultural event held in communities across Ontario. For one special weekend, cities open the doors to historic buildings, cultural institutions, churches, theatres, and other interesting spaces—many of which are normally closed to the public.\nVisitors can explore at their own pace, learn about local history, and sometimes go behind the scenes with guided tours or special access.\n\nLearn more about the event here:\n👉 [https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/niagara-on-the-lake](https://www.doorsopenontario.on.ca/pages/events/niagara-on-the-lake)\n\n***\n\n### 🗓️ The Plan\n\n* **Departure:** 8:00 AM from just outside **Christie Station**\n* **Transportation:** Rental minivan or SUV\n* **Destination:** **Niagara-on-the-Lake**\n* Spend the day exploring **Doors Open sites around town**\n* Time permitting we may be able to visit Niagara Falls after for a few photos/sightseeing\n* **Return to Toronto:** Around **6:00 PM**, depending on traffic\n\nYou’re welcome to explore with the group or wander off to check out sites that interest you most. The day will be relaxed and flexible.\n\n***\n\n### 🍽️ Food & Drink\n\nYou are responsible for **your own food and drink purchases** throughout the day.\n\n***\n\n### 💰 Cost\n\n**$60 round-trip**\nThis covers:\n\n* Car rental\n* Insurance\n* Fuel\n\nTo secure your spot, **all participants must e-transfer $60 to:**\n📧 **[nicolasbello@yahoo.com](mailto:nicolasbello@yahoo.com)**\nSpots are limited based on vehicle capacity, so please RSVP only if you’re able to commit.\n\n***\n\n### 🌦️ Weather Note\n\nThis event **runs rain or shine**, so please **dress appropriately for the weather**. The good news is that we’ll be **inside most of the time**, but there will still be some walking between locations.\n\n***\n\n### 🎒 What to Bring\n\n* Comfortable walking shoes\n* Curiosity & good vibes\n* A little patience for traffic (it’s part of the road-trip charm!)\n\nJoin us for a fun architectural adventure and a chance to explore one of Ontario’s most historic towns. 🚐🏛️","startDate":"2026-10-17T12:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Christie Station","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Bloor and Christie, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-movies-and-social-group/"},"performer":"Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Community Wim Hof practice","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-wim-hof-method-meetup-group/events/316734709/","description":"It's better when we're together. Come and experience the power of the WHM with a wonderful group of people. We breathe, we go into the cold and we teach our bodies to heat up properly. We develop resilience and the mindset to use these powerful healing tools over and over again, all year round. This gathering is fully guided by Wim Hof instructor Steve Beattie.\n\nIf you are new to this, come on down, enjoy the support and practice in a safe way with us. If you already have a WHM practice this meetup is a great way to take it to the next level, and make lots of new friends.\n\nThere will be a fire, snacks and drinks shared by other attendees. We have been doing this 6 for years!\n\n**What to bring?**\n\n* Yoga mat\n* Weather-appropriate clothing (better to dress too warm!)\n* Bathing suite, towel\n* Water shoes (optional)\n\nIn extreme weather being prepared is very important. Especially if it's your first time, please read up on how to come prepared [here.](https://www.breathinginnature.com/wim-hof-method-meetup/)\n\nLearn more about our Wim Hof meetups, workshops, breath classes, wilderness trips, medicine work and special events at **[Breathing in Nature](https://breathinginnature.com/)**.\n\nJoin the \"**[Wim Hof Toronto](https://www.facebook.com/groups/1714218015474146/)**\" group on Facebook to see all of our local events.\n\nThis is a free event made possible by our Gift Economy. You can learn more about the Gift Economy [here](https://breathinginnature.com/gift-economy/).","startDate":"2026-10-17T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Humber Bay Park-West","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Humber Bay Park Road W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Wim Hof Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-wim-hof-method-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Wim Hof Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Pickleball Beginner Skills & Play (15+): Oct 17-31 - $135/3 Classes","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/events/316504818/","description":"📅 **Registration Required in Advance**\nRSVP’ing on Meetup does **not** reserve your spot.\n👉[ ](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=kMQ2BO5)**[Register here](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=kMQ2BO5)**\n☎️ Or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\nSpaces are limited to ensure personalized instruction — early registration is encouraged!\n\n***\n\n## Pickleball Beginner Skills & Play (15+) at the Miles Nadal JCC\n\nHave you tried pickleball and want to feel more confident on the court? This **Beginner Skills & Play** program is the perfect next step!\n\nDesigned for players with **some familiarity** with pickleball, this small-group program helps you build a strong foundation through guided instruction, skill development, and beginner-friendly gameplay. Each session blends coaching, drills, and structured play so you can apply what you’re learning right away in a supportive, low-pressure environment.\n\n🏓 **What You’ll Work On:**\n\n* Review of basic rules, scoring, and court positioning\n* Developing proper technique for serves, returns, volleys, and rallies\n* Introductory doubles strategy and on-court decision-making\n* Applying skills through structured practice games\n* Individualized feedback and interactive Q&A with the instructor\n\n***\n\n📍 **Location:** Miles Nadal JCC — 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through Spadina doors)\n👥 **Format:** Small-group instruction led by an experienced, friendly coach\n🎾 **Equipment:** Paddles and balls are provided (or bring your own)\n\n***\n\n🧡 **Why Join?**\n\n* Build confidence and consistency in your game\n* Learn in a welcoming, beginner-friendly environment\n* Get comfortable playing real games, not just drills\n* A great bridge between Intro clinics and Drop-In play\n\n🔔 **New to pickleball?**\nIf you’ve never played before, we recommend starting with our **Intro to Pickleball Clinic**.\n\nWhether you’re looking to play recreationally, improve your skills, or prepare for more regular play, this program will help you feel confident stepping onto the court. Come learn, play, and have fun! 🏓","startDate":"2026-10-17T13:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal JCC","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave - M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-miles-nadal-jcc-sports-and-recreation/"},"performer":"Drop-in Recreation - Volleyball, Basketball & Pickleball"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Saturday Beach Volleyball","url":"https://www.meetup.com/brampton-volleyball-meetup-group/events/316734505/","description":"**NO SHOWS are STRICTLY NOT ALLOWED as it impacts the game so please respect your RSVPs**\n\nWelcome to **Season 4 of Outdoor Volleyball**\n\nWednesday Evening (Mahaffy Park - Grass Court)\nSaturday Morning (Chinguacousy Park - Sand Court)\n\n**FEES: Your first volleyball game with the group is FREE! Come check out the group, meet the players, and see if it’s a good fit for you.**\n\n**To confirm you spot, E-Transfer** to mech.swapnil@gmail.com.\n\n**2026 Remaining Season Fees per player- $20 (Aug to October)**\n**Drop-in Fee per player - $5 per day**\n\n**If payment is not received, you will be put on the waitlist.**","startDate":"2026-10-17T13:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Chinguacousy Park Brampton","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Brampton","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Donald M. Gordon Chinguacousy Park, 9050 Bramalea Rd, Brampton, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Brampton Volleyball and Social Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/brampton-volleyball-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Brampton Volleyball and Social Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"All-Level &Beginner Friendly $10 Drop In Saturday Morning @ CA Badminton ","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/events/316332800/","description":":Saturday Morning Drop In\nCost $ 10 \\*\\*\\*\n\\* Included Plastic birdies, please try to have cash and pay before playing.\n\\*\\*\\*(Cash Only) (Cash Only) (Cash Only)\n\nLocation: 1370 Birchmount Rd, Unit 6\n\\*The close intersection in Birchmount Rd & Lawrence Ave.\nTime: Saturday 9:30 AM - 12 PM\n\\*\\*\\*9:30 AM- 12 PM 3 courts available\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\n\\*Please bring your own racquet,\n\\*Please bring indoor gym sport shoes. (Change shoes in the club)\n\\*\\*\\*\n\\*This weekly gathering is for all levels (beginner to advance) badminton players.\n\\*No outside food allowed.\n\\* This event is for the purpose of playing friendly double games and for all levels of players from beginner to advance. Please do not use this as an opportunity to do training and singles games.\nAttendance in effect -please give at least 24hr notice in advance for cancelation so others may have time to react. Late show and no-shows maybe permanently removed from group and unable to rejoin.\n\\*Only registered members can participate; visitors are not permitted. If you wish to participate, please register as a member first, and then view the event details and participation instructions.\n\n\\*\\*\\*\\*\\*\\* ⚠️⚠️⚠️\nTo ensure efficient use of event slots and fairness, all registered participants must confirm their attendance with the group administrator before the specified deadline (if a waitlist exists). \\* Before the deadline, registered members have the right to cancel and priority. To ensure fairness, if no response is received after the deadline, the waiting list member has priority.\n\nIf you do not confirm your attendance within 72 hours before the event, or are absent, your slot may be reassigned to a waiting list candidate or a new member. This rule aims to ensure fairness and maximize the participation opportunities for all members. Since the venue cost is shared by all confirmed participants, 🛎️ those who do not attend must notify the administrator before the deadline. Failure to notify the administrator before the deadline will result in payment of the venue cost. Thank you for your understanding. \\*Please note: Failure to pay the venue cost will result in your cancellation of membership.\n\nSlot allocation is based on the order of candidate responses. To ensure fairness and better coordination, when a registered candidate cancels their slot, the administrator will send a separate notification to all candidates each time slots open. Due to limited availability, places will be allocated on a first-come, first-served basis based on response time.\n\n\\*If you need to cancel your participation, please notify the administrator at least 24 hours before the event. Late cancellations will incur venue fees. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n\\*To ensure fairness and transparency, each participant needs to confirm individually. Members who fail to cancel their registration and complete payment within the specified time will be permanently disqualified.\n\nPlease note that if you confirm participation on behalf of another member, you will be responsible for that member's event costs.\n\nTo maintain fairness for all participants, please inform your friends that they must also confirm.\n\n\\*In the event of repeated violations, the administrator reserves the right to make the final decision.\n\nThank you for your understanding and cooperation.\n\n* After reading the event details, members can contact the administrator via message.","startDate":"2026-10-17T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"CA Badminton Academy","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Scarborough","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1370 Birchmount rd, unit 6, Scarborough, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ca-badminton-meetup-toronto-group-gta/"},"performer":"CA Badminton Meetup Toronto Group GTA"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FRC Toronto :: Saturday Run","url":"https://www.meetup.com/founders-running-club-toronto/events/316734904/","description":"**Founders Running Club** (FRC) brings founders, investors, tech, creative people and startup enthusiasts together for weekly easy runs and networking. We like to be comfortable when we run and finish with coffee and conversations. Choose your pace or follow a pacer—pets, friends, family, are welcome.\n\n🗓️ Launched in San Francisco, July 16, 2022\n🌍 Now in 35+ cities\n📅 Running + Networking events + Community\n\n**Join the community** https://bit.ly/frc-toronto-chat\n\n**Stay updated**:\nInstagram [http://instagram.com/foundersrc/](http://instagram.com/foundersrc/)\nPodcast [http://podcast.foundersrc.com/](http://podcast.foundersrc.com/)\nLinkedIn [http://linkedin.com/company/foundersrc/](http://linkedin.com/company/foundersrc/)\nStrava [http://strava.com/clubs/foundersRC](http://strava.com/clubs/foundersRC)\nWebsite [http://foundersrc.com/](http://foundersrc.com/)","startDate":"2026-10-17T13:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","event